<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kalgoorlie</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kalgoorlie is a city in the Goldfields of Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, founded after Paddy Hannan found gold there in June 1893. The Golden Mile, one of the richest gold-bearing areas in the world, made it the centre of the region, and a pipeline from near Perth, opened in 1903, supplied it with water. The huge Super Pit open-cut mine still operates there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kalgoorlie.jpg" alt="Kalgoorlie" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kalgoorlie_Post_Office_DSC04483.JPG: Original uploader was Yewenyi at en.wikipedia derivative work: Original uploader... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kalgoorlie.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
